{%- comment -%}
  The trust row under the accordions.

  It was hard-wired to exactly two cards in a `1fr 1fr` grid, so the third
  merchant-owned promise the rest of the theme already prints (the cart page
  shows returns + shipping + money-back) had nowhere to go, and adding it by
  hand dropped a lone card onto a second row. The row is now count-driven:
  it renders however many of the three lines the merchant actually filled in,
  and publishes the number as data-trust-count so the stylesheet can set the
  column count from one attribute instead of a media-query guess.

  EVERY LINE IS MERCHANT-OWNED AND PRINTS VERBATIM. Empty stays empty — the
  settings document "empty = the line does not render", and the theme must not
  substitute a locale default here: a translated storefront would then advertise
  a money-back guarantee the merchant never wrote. No claim is invented and
  nothing is timed, counted down or framed as running out.

  The audit found second lines clipped. The markup fix is here — each claim is
  its own element with nothing forcing it onto one line — and the rest is the
  stylesheet's: the cards must size to their tallest content, never to a fixed
  height, and the count must not squeeze three cards into two columns.

  Params: none (reads settings directly, like the pair it replaces)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign tr_back = settings.guarantee_line
  assign tr_ship = settings.ship_free_line
  assign tr_ret = settings.trust_returns_line

  assign tr_count = 0
  if tr_back != blank
    assign tr_count = tr_count | plus: 1
  endif
  if tr_ship != blank
    assign tr_count = tr_count | plus: 1
  endif
  if tr_ret != blank
    assign tr_count = tr_count | plus: 1
  endif
-%}
{%- if tr_count > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%} .pdp-trust-duo is kept alongside the new name: it is the class the
  shipped stylesheet already paints, and dropping it would strip the cards bare on
  any store that updates the theme before the stylesheet. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="pdp-trust-duo pdp-trust-row lbl-sm" data-trust-count="{{ tr_count }}">
    {%- if tr_back != blank -%}
      <span class="pdp-trust-row__item">{% render 'icon', name: 'returns', size: 20 %}<em>{{ tr_back | escape }}</em></span>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if tr_ship != blank -%}
      <span class="pdp-trust-row__item">{% render 'icon', name: 'truck', size: 20 %}<em>{{ tr_ship | escape }}</em></span>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if tr_ret != blank -%}
      <span class="pdp-trust-row__item">{% render 'icon', name: 'check', size: 20 %}<em>{{ tr_ret | escape }}</em></span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
